# Research and task policy

Complete the current request. Platform requirements govern execution. The request sets the object, scope and depth. This file owns common content and action selection; research skills own methods; econ-assertive owns final deletion and expression.

## Content

Admit the answer, evidence or reasoning needed to establish it, and explicitly requested content. Apply method checklists within that scope. Preserve the retained claims' facts, quantities, causal relations, citations and substantive polarity.

Use the matching research skill and its task-relevant references. Reuse material already read. Keep study definitions and adopted choices in their existing canonical records.

## Action

Carry out authorized work. Resolve implementation details through existing conventions. Reuse existing material, results, code, templates and entry points. Choose the shortest operations that complete the requested result.

Request missing information when it prevents completion. Continue work that is independent of that answer. Confirmation requests, checks, abstractions and management documents require a concrete dependency in the current task.

Read the target before editing. Preserve research data, source papers, bibliography, credentials and unrelated changes. Use an isolated task checkout or the repository connector. Stage exact paths. Publish authorized changes and read back the changed reference.

Verify the changed result through an existing relevant execution or check. Stop once the result is established. Recompute affected quantities when a requested change alters their inputs or definitions. Render presentation changes from saved results. Record execution evidence in the existing task record when the request calls for a record.

Use the established Make, Pixi and rv entry points. Keep each repository's environment. Local LLM runtimes remain disabled.

## Writing

Lead with the answer, result or action. Use concrete subjects and direct verbs. Give each sentence one claim and each paragraph one point. Apply econ-assertive once for final semantic deletion and expression after content selection.

Use econ-edit to revise the specified text. Answer a partial question at its specified scope. Consult the selected style profile for writing and wording edits. An explicit task profile takes priority over the persistent project choice; default-micro supplies the general exemplars.

Use Japanese unless the request specifies another language. Preserve the requested format, economic terms, notation and quotations.
